    "lawCode": "Amd §265.20, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4922B\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to the sale and possession of\nself-defense spray devices\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRelates to the sale and possession of self-defense spray devices in the\nstate.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the penal law to permit the shipping and sale of self-\ndefense spray devices within the state.\n\nSection 2. Repeals a portion of the penal taw, which specified that the\n\"possession and sale of a self-defense spray device\" could only be\nperformed by a licensed firearms dealer or a licensed pharmacist who was\nauthorized and approved by the superintendent of state police.\n\nSection 3. Set an effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nThe B print removes language requiring that Department of Health regu-\nlations allow the devices to be shipped into the state and limits the\nnumber of devices that may be sold at any one time to a single purchas-\ner.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSelf-defense spray devices, such as pepper spray, can be a powerful tool\nagainst attackers. With the threat of violence against women remaining a\nconcern, giving people a non-lethal tool to defend themselves from their\nwould-be attackers and escape from the situation could be lifesaving.\nPepper spray is legal in New York state, but there are numerous\nrestrictions. Streamlining the regulations will make it easier for New\nYorkers to obtain these important self-defense devices.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-24 A8140: Referred to Codes\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
